concept strings {
  name     = "Strings"
  summary  = "UTF-8 by default, with encoding prefixes, heredocs, and opt-in interpolation."
  related  = [string_literals, string_escapes, heredocs, raw_heredocs, string_interpolation, symbols, expressions]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p <<PROSE
String literals are UTF-8 by default. A prefix selects another encoding; heredocs
offer multi-line and verbatim variants; a `$` prefix opts the string into
expression interpolation. String builtins (split, join, replace, contains, slice,
and so on) are covered in the String functions reference.
PROSE
    p "- [String Literals](concept_string_literals) — UTF-8 by default plus `ascii`/`utf16`/`utf32` prefixes."
    p "- [String Escapes](concept_string_escapes) — backslash escapes inside double-quoted strings."
    p "- [Heredocs](concept_heredocs) — `<<TAG ... TAG` multi-line strings with escapes and indentation stripping."
    p "- [Raw Heredocs](concept_raw_heredocs) — single-quoted tag takes the body verbatim."
    p "- [String Interpolation](concept_string_interpolation) — opt-in `$` prefix with `${ ... }` slots."
  }
}
